       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets. Metformin at that level raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and I can't enter a dose above the labeled maximum.\n\nIf the intent was within the labeled range, I can enter one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This totals 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting dose, which is then titrated up.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If you meant 1700 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter it as 850 mg twice daily. I can also add a note to the order, such as \"hold for contrast or acute kidney injury.\""
      }
